From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sta: ArrivalVisitor copy keeps clks_only
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

BfsIterator::visitParallel visits a level with one copy of the arrival
visitor per thread, and the copy constructor passed false for
clks_only. With more than one thread, findClkArrivals
(Sta::ensureClkArrivals) did not stop at register clock pins and searched
the whole design instead of the clock network. Every caller paid for it:
report_clock_skew, report_clock_latency, the min pulse width checks,
write_timing_model, the web viewer's clock tree, and with 0207 CTS
latency balancing. The clock arrivals found are the same.

Upstream as The-OpenROAD-Project/OpenSTA#462; retires with the //:bump
onto an OpenROAD whose OpenSTA has it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
---
diff --git a/src/sta/search/Search.cc b/src/sta/search/Search.cc
index ea4b6db7..5abf594b 100644
--- a/src/sta/search/Search.cc
+++ b/src/sta/search/Search.cc
@@ -1147,7 +1147,9 @@ ArrivalVisitor::ArrivalVisitor(const ArrivalVisitor &arrival_visitor) :
   filtered_arrivals_(new VertexSeq)
 {
   init0();
-  init(arrival_visitor.always_to_endpoints_, false, arrival_visitor.pred_);
+  init(arrival_visitor.always_to_endpoints_,
+       arrival_visitor.clks_only_,
+       arrival_visitor.pred_);
 }
 
 void
